'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-goertzel-sinc2-iteration-count.spin2
''   Purpose.... Reproduce, measure and explain the streamer Goertzel SINC2
''               corruption that a varying NCO-cycle length causes
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Sep 2026
''   Updated.... 25 Sep 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS TESTED
    Chip Gracey (P2 designer), 2024-12-16, Silicon Doc note of the same date:
    in the streamer's Goertzel SINC2 mode, "When the number of clocks varies
    from the norm to complete a full NCO cycle, the X and Y values coming from
    GETXACC will be off by one double integration and it will corrupt the
    computed sample, along with the next one, before correcting." Cause: a
    SETXFRQ value that is not a power of two. Fixes: a power-of-two count;
    SINC1 is not sensitive; XZERO (not XCONT) with a period under ~20 ms "may
    be fine". Diagnostic: "WAITX #1 WC" before GETXACC gives "huge noise".
    Source: engineering/ingestion/external-inputs/forum-threads/
    ProblemGoertzelSINC2mode/INGEST.md; silicon-doc-text.txt:1606-1705.

    Five questions, both outcomes of each fixed below before the run:
    Q1 reproduce   Q2 SINC1 contrast   Q3 WAITX #1 WC diagnostic
    Q4 XZERO       Q5 mechanism (a value-for-value accumulator model)

  RIG
    Any P2 board, NO jumper, nothing attached to P3; P0..P7 free. The
    measuring cog drives P3 itself (WRPIN 0, DIR=1): LOW for half of the
    calibration, then HIGH for everything else. P3 is the Goertzel input
    4g+3 of pin group g = 0. TESTP checks the level in every phase. No DAC
    output anywhere (mode bits [11:8] = 0). P56..P63 are not touched.
    _clkfreq = 200 MHz (the campaign's proven rig).

  DEBUGGER (EF-057)
    DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001. All streamer work and every GETXACC runs in a
    dedicated PASM cog started by COGINIT from the DAT block below; cog 0
    only reads the hub mailbox and reports.

  STIMULUS, AND WHY A CONSTANT TERM (not a cosine table)
    Every one of the 512 LUT longs is $0301_0000 (cos byte [23:16] = 1, sin
    byte [31:24] = 3), P3 is held, and S = $0000_8000 sums P3 only. So every
    active clock adds the same term C: C_X = +1, C_Y = +3 with P3 HIGH
    (EF-070's sign rule, imm[19] = 0). With C constant every quantity below
    is an exact integer that depends only on how many clocks each read
    window held, so every reading can be predicted to the count. With C_X =
    1 an X reading literally counts clocks. A cosine table with a DC input
    would make each clean sample depend on the per-clock LUT index sequence,
    which drifts under a non-power-of-two SETXFRQ: only a clock-by-clock NCO
    simulation could predict it, so Q5 could not be decided exactly. The
    corruption Chip describes is a property of the window lengths, and a
    constant term exposes window lengths exactly. Y = 3 * X must hold in every
    sample (corroboration: a second, independent accumulator).

  THE READ LOOP (Chip's Silicon Doc demo shape)
      XCONT cmd,S / WAITX #1 / GETXACC x / MOV y,0-0 / GETCT ct / 3 x WRLONG
    XCONT waits for the prior command's last clock (silicon-doc-text:1407),
    so each GETXACC lands a fixed number of clocks after a command boundary
    and the read-to-read window equals one command's length. GETCT, taken a
    fixed 4 clocks after each GETXACC, measures every window: L_k = ct_k -
    ct_(k-1). Chip's SINC2 sample is the difference of successive reads,
    d_k = x_k - x_(k-1) (his demo: "if SINC2, get differences").
    Q3 variant: WAITX #1 WC (2 + (1 AND RND) clocks) in the same place.
    Q4 variant: XZERO instead of XCONT.
    Before every arm: a SINC1 zero burst (S[15:12] = 0, count 4, F = 1:1)
    sets the first stage to 0 (SINC1 REPLACES it: silicon-doc-text:1610),
    then SETXFRQ <arm F> with the streamer idle, then XINIT (zeroes phase).
    Samples k < WARM = 3 are start-up and are not analysed.

  SETXFRQ ARITHMETIC (NCO: phase = (phase & $7FFF_FFFF) + F; the count in
  D[15:0] is NCO rollovers, so one command = M cycles; under XCONT the mean
  command length is exactly M * 2^31 / F clocks)
    P2   F = $0080_0000 = 2^23: 2^31 / F = 256 exactly. M = 8 -> every
         command 2048 clocks (10.24 us). No variation, ever.
    NPS  F = $0080_0040 = 8_388_672 = 2^23 + 64, M = 8:
         8 * 2^31 / F = 17_179_869_184 / 8_388_672 = 2048 - 131_072/8_388_672
         = 2047.98437512 -> windows 2048, one 2047 every 64.0005 commands
         = 655.4 us.  (dl = -1: one clock SHORT)
    NPL  F = $007F_FFC0 = 8_388_544 = 2^23 - 64, M = 8:
         2048 + 131_072/8_388_544 = 2048.01562512 -> one 2049 every 63.9990
         commands = 655.4 us.  (dl = +1: one clock LONG)
    CHP  F = $00A3_D70C = 10_737_420 (1,000,000.19 Hz at 200 MHz), M = 100
         (Chip's 100-cycle measurements): 100 * 2^31 / F = 214_748_364_800 /
         10_737_420 = 20000 - 35_200/10_737_420 = 19_999.996722 -> windows
         20000 (100 us), one 19_999 every 305.04 commands = 30.50 ms: inside
         Chip's "30-60 ms per error". (The Silicon Doc +1 rounding rule's
         1 MHz value $00A3_D70B = 10_737_419 gives one every 706.4 commands
         = 70.6 ms.) 2048 samples = 204.8 ms -> about 6-7 events.
    LONG F = FREQ_CHIP, M = 25_000: 25_000 * 2^31 / F = 4_999_999.18044 ->
         windows 4_999_999 (25 ms), one 5_000_000 every 5.54 commands =
         138.6 ms.  (dl = +1)
    XZERO phase is zeroed at every command start, so every command repeats the
         same rollover pattern: ONE window length. Predicted ceil(M*2^31/F)
         = 2048 / 20000 / 5_000_000 if the first add falls on the command's
         first clock (silicon-doc-text:1409); only constancy is predicted.
    The program recomputes all of these from F and M (pred_windows) and
    prints them before the run's data.

  ARMS (run order; all P3 HIGH; samples = GETXACC reads)
    #  name    mode  loop                 F      M       samples  role
    0  P2-S1   SINC1 XCONT                P2     8       1024     CONTROL
    1  P2-S2   SINC2 XCONT                P2     8       1024     Q1 clean, Q5
    2  NPS-S1  SINC1 XCONT                NPS    8       1024     Q2
    3  NPS-S2  SINC2 XCONT                NPS    8       1024     Q1, Q5
    4  NPL-S1  SINC1 XCONT                NPL    8       1024     Q2
    5  NPL-S2  SINC2 XCONT                NPL    8       1024     Q1, Q5
    6  CHP-S1  SINC1 XCONT                CHP    100     2048     Q2
    7  CHP-S2  SINC2 XCONT                CHP    100     2048     Q1 cadence, Q5
    8  JIT-S1  SINC1 XCONT + WAITX #1 WC  P2     8       1024     Q3
    9  JIT-S2  SINC2 XCONT + WAITX #1 WC  P2     8       1024     Q3, Q5
    10 XZS-S2  SINC2 XZERO                NPS    8       1024     Q4 (twin 3)
    11 XZC-S2  SINC2 XZERO                CHP    100     2048     Q4 (twin 7)
    12 XZL-S2  SINC2 XZERO                CHP    25_000  16       Q4 25 ms
    13 XCL-S2  SINC2 XCONT                CHP    25_000  16       Q4 twin of 12

  THE CARRY MODEL (Q5) -- built only from what is proven or documented:
    EF-070: xsum adds, on each active clock, the value the first stage held
            BEFORE that clock's edge (a one-clock trail).
    Silicon Doc: SINC1 first stage := term; SINC2 first stage += term (the
            same register accumulates: a running integral).
    EF-069: GETXACC during an active Goertzel command returns xsum and
            zeroes it, partitioning the terms exactly; it does not clear the
            first stage (Silicon Doc: SIN_ACC/COS_ACC are what it clears).
    Let window k hold n_k = L_k - g active clocks (g = clocks per window that
    add nothing; measured by P2-S1, expected 0) and J_k = the first-stage
    value xsum adds on window k's first clock. With a constant term C:
        x_k     = n_k*J_k + C*n_k*(n_k-1)/2
        J_(k+1) = J_k + C*n_k
        d_k     = x_k - x_(k-1)
    Equal windows n:  d_k = C*n^2 exactly, whatever J is (the clean value).
    One window of n+dl (dl = +-1) between windows of n:
        e_k     = d_k - C*n^2     =  dl*J_(k-1) + 2*C*n*dl + C*(dl^2-dl)/2
        e_(k+1)                   = -dl*J_(k-1) - dl*n*C  - C*(dl^2-dl)/2
        e_(k+2) = 0               (self-corrects)       e_k + e_(k+1) = dl*n*C
    Each member of the pair is about +-J: one first-stage (double-
    integration) value gained or lost by a window one clock longer or
    shorter, then handed back by the next sample. SINC1 has no differencing
    and no running first stage: x_k = C*n_k, so the odd window reads exactly
    dl*C off, alone.
    Numbers with C = +1 (J_(k-1) ~ 2048*k: at most ~131_000 at the first
    NPS/NPL pair, ~2_100_000 by k = 1023; d0 = 4_194_304):
      NPS (n = 2048, dl = -1):  e_k = -(J + 4095)   e_(k+1) = J + 2047   sum -2048
      NPL (n = 2048, dl = +1):  e_k =   J + 4096    e_(k+1) = -(J + 2048) sum +2048
      CHP (n = 20000, dl = -1): e_k = -(J + 39_999) e_(k+1) = J + 19_999 sum -20000
                                (d0 = 400_000_000)
    The program fits J ONCE per SINC2 arm, at k = 3, from x_3 = n*J +
    C*n(n-1)/2 (the division must be exact), then predicts every later x_k,
    d_k and e_k from the measured windows alone, and prints predicted beside
    measured for every outlier and its neighbours.
    What the one-clock lag itself contributes cannot be isolated in a
    continuous stream: it shifts every J by one C, which the fit absorbs.
    What Q5 decides is whether the accumulator structure EF-069/EF-070
    belong to reproduces the corruption value for value.
    Named alternatives and what they would show:
      first stage cleared by GETXACC  -> clean d is not C*n^2 (d ~ 0)
      a term dropped or doubled at a varying boundary -> outlier residual
                                         x_k - x^_k = +-C or +-J, clean rows exact
      first stage narrower than 32 bits -> a CLEAN row stops matching once J
                                         passes its range (J is printed)

  PREDICTIONS AND VERDICT RULES (fixed before the run)
  Outlier: a SINC2 sample with d_k <> C*n^2 (n = the arm's usual window).
  Window-changed sample: n_k or n_(k-1) differs from the usual window.
    Q1  CONFIRMED  P2-S2 has 0 outliers; NPS-S2, NPL-S2 and CHP-S2 each show
                   >= 2 complete runs, every outlier sits on a window change,
                   every window change corrupts, and every run is exactly an
                   adjacent pair (odd window, then the next) followed by a
                   clean sample. Rate: 2 samples per odd window (NPS/NPL 2 in
                   64 = 3.1 %, CHP 2 in 305).
        REFUTED    P2-S2 has an outlier; or NPS-S2/NPL-S2 has none; or a
                   window change leaves d clean; or runs are not pairs.
        INCONCLUSIVE  an arm failed its window control; an outlier with no
                   window change (another cause); fewer than 2 runs.
    Q2  CONFIRMED  in NPS-S1, NPL-S1, CHP-S1 every sample equals C*(L_k - g)
                   and the odd window reads exactly one term (+-C, 1/n) off,
                   alone -- no double-integration outlier, no pair.
        REFUTED    a SINC1 sample differs from C*(L_k - g), or deviates by
                   more than one term.
    Q3  CONFIRMED  jitter present (windows D-1/D/D+1); JIT-S2 has >= 25 % of
                   samples off by >= 1000 terms (predicted ~75 % corrupted if
                   the RND bits are independent: n_k <> n_(k-1) in 6 of 8 bit
                   patterns; |e| ~ J = 8_000 .. 2_100_000); JIT-S1 deviates
                   by at most one term (predicted +-1 in ~50 %); and the same
                   loop without WC (P2-S2) is clean.
        REFUTED    JIT-S2 < 5 % huge; or JIT-S1 off by more than one term.
    Q4  CONFIRMED  XZS-S2, XZC-S2, XZL-S2 each keep ONE window length and
                   every SINC2 sample d equals the first (d(k=4)), while their
                   XCONT twins (3, 7, 13) show odd windows and outliers;
                   window tested: 10.24 us, 100 us and 25 ms measurements
                   over 10.5 / 204.8 / 400 ms streams. (Constancy, not
                   C*n^2, is the XZERO test: g is measured on an XCONT loop;
                   d(k=4) is printed beside C*n^2.)
        REFUTED    an XZERO arm shows window variation.
        INCONCLUSIVE  constant windows but changed samples (a different
                   mechanism -- first-stage range at that J); a twin without
                   odd windows.
    Q5  CARRY-MODEL-MATCHES  in P2-S2, NPS-S2, NPL-S2 and JIT-S2 the fit is
                   exact and every sample -- clean and outlier, >= 16 outliers
                   -- equals the model value exactly.
        SEPARATE-MECHANISM  outlier samples differ from the model while every
                   clean-window sample matches (residuals printed); or the
                   clean prediction C*n^2 fails everywhere in P2-S2.
        INCONCLUSIVE  fit failed; a clean-window sample broke the model
                   (premise failure: J printed); too few outliers.
    CHP-S2, XZS-S2, XZC-S2 corroborate Q5 (J reaches ~2^25 there).

  IN-RUN CONTROLS (a failure prints RIG FAIL and withholds verdicts)
    LUT   : all 512 LUT longs read back = $0301_0000.
    CAL   : SINC1 at F = 1:1, the EF-070 flush idiom (zero burst, 64-clock
            burst, zero burst): R - B = 64*C. |C_X| = 1, C_Y = 3*C_X, and C
            flips sign with P3 (proves the term comes from P3).
    PIN   : TESTP = the driven level at CAL and at every arm start and end.
    LOCK  : P2-S1 and P2-S2: every window = 2048 clocks (the loop is locked to
            command boundaries); P2-S1: every x equal, x/C whole, g = 2048 -
            x/C within +-2 (the power-of-two SINC1 stream is perfectly steady).
    SIZE  : the engine's per-arm sample count echo = the table.
    SPREAD: per arm, window max - min <= 1 (<= 2 for the jitter arms), else
            that arm's verdicts are withheld (RIG FAIL line names it).

  DEPENDS ON CLAIMS NOT VERIFIED ON SILICON
    - SINC2's first stage is the register SINC1 replaces (Silicon Doc names
      one SIN_MUL/COS_MUL for both), so the SINC1 zero burst zeroes it before
      each arm. Not assumed by the model: J is fitted; J/C is printed beside
      the clock count from XINIT so a carried-in value is visible.
    - First stage and xsum wrap as 32-bit registers (the model is mod 2^32).
      J reaches ~2^21 (fast arms), ~2^25.3 (CHP), ~2^26.3 (25 ms arms).
    - XCONT/XZERO release on the prior command's last clock (Silicon Doc):
      checked by the LOCK control and measured per sample by GETCT.
    - Seamless chaining (no dead clock): measured as g, gated, used.
    - XZERO zeroes phase per command: the Q4 prediction itself.
    - WAITX #1 WC = 2 + (1 AND RND) (p2kb waitx): jitter-presence check.
    - MULDIV64 signedness: the Spin2 v55 doc says unsigned, the KB says
      signed; every operand here is kept positive, so it does not matter.

  VERIFIED ENCODINGS (pnut-ts v1.55.8, `pnut-ts -d -l`, decoded from the .lst
  hex dump; engine at object offset $2E8 = cog $000, data longs at cog
  $082..$087, arm_tab at cog $088 = offset $508):
    XINIT dzero_,imz_    $FCA10887  [27:21]=1100101 [20]=0 (XINIT) L=I=0,
                                    D=$084 (dzero_) S=$087 (imz_)
    XINIT dcal_,imk_     $FCA10A86  D=$085 (dcal_) S=$086 (imk_)
    XINIT dcmd_,imk_     $FCA18E86  D=$0C7 (dcmd_) S=$086 -- arm start
    XCONT dcmd_,imk_     $FCC18E86  [27:21]=1100110 [20]=0 L=I=0 (loop_xc,
                                    loop_jit)
    XZERO dcmd_,imk_     $FCB18E86  [27:21]=1100101 [20]=1 L=I=0 (loop_xz)
    XSTOP                $FCAC0000  = XINIT #0,#0 (L=I=1, D=S=0)
    WAITX #1             $FD64021F  C=Z=0, L=1, D=1: a fixed 3 clocks
    WAITX #1 WC          $FD74021F  C=1: 2 + (1 AND RND) clocks (loop_jit
                                    only; the one word the loops differ in,
                                    besides XCONT/XZERO)
    GETXACC xsum_        $FD619E1E  [27:21]=1101011 [8:0]=000011110, D=$0CF;
                                    next word MOV ysum_,0-0 = $F601A000 (S=0)
    GETXACC calb_ / calr_  $FD61A41E / $FD61A81E, each followed by MOV x,0-0
    GETCT ctv_ / ct0_    $FD61A21A / $FD61981A
    SETXFRQ freq1to1_    $FD61041D  [8:0]=000011101, D=$082
    SETXFRQ armf_        $FD618C1D  D=$0C6
    WRLUT lutv_,idx_ $FC3106C1 | RDLUT tmp_,idx_ $FAA184C1 | SETLUTS #0
    $FD640037 | WRPIN #0,#3 $FC0C0003 | DRVL #3 $FD640658 | DRVH #3
    $FD640659 | TESTP #3 WC $FD740640
    ALTS rowp_ $F9958A00 (S=#0), then MOV x,0-0; no AUGS precedes any ALTx
    (EF-066). No SETQ anywhere in the engine.
    DAT longs, byte for byte: freq1to1_ $8000_0000, lutv_ $0301_0000,
      dzero_ $F007_0004, dcal_ $F007_0040, imk_ $0000_8000, imz_ $0000_0000
    arm_tab rows (F, D, kind, samples), in ARM_xxx order:
      $0080_0000 $F007_0008 0 1024 | $0080_0000 $F087_0008 0 1024
      $0080_0040 $F007_0008 0 1024 | $0080_0040 $F087_0008 0 1024
      $007F_FFC0 $F007_0008 0 1024 | $007F_FFC0 $F087_0008 0 1024
      $00A3_D70C $F007_0064 0 2048 | $00A3_D70C $F087_0064 0 2048
      $0080_0000 $F007_0008 1 1024 | $0080_0000 $F087_0008 1 1024
      $0080_0040 $F087_0008 2 1024 | $00A3_D70C $F087_0064 2 2048
      $00A3_D70C $F087_61A8 2 16   | $00A3_D70C $F087_61A8 0 16
    Mode words: D[31:16] = $F007 -> mode [15:12]=1111, [11:8]=0000 (no DAC),
      [7]=0 (SINC1), [6:3]=0000 (pin group 0), [2:0]=111; $F087 is identical
      with [7]=1 (SINC2). Counts: $0008 = 8, $0064 = 100, $61A8 = 25_000,
      $0004 (zero burst), $0040 = 64 (CAL).

  HOW TO RUN
    Compile: pnut-ts -d test-goertzel-sinc2-iteration-count.spin2
    Load with pnut-term-ts (or PNut) with DEBUG enabled. The engine runs
    about 1.6 s; the report prints several hundred lines. Success looks like:
    no RIG FAIL lines, five "VERDICT Q..." lines, then "=== END ===".
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq        = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS      = %0000_0001            ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY
  CLK_MHZ         = 200                   ' clocks per microsecond at _clkfreq

  PIN             = 3                     ' Goertzel input 4g+3, pin group g = 0
  G_COS           = 1                     ' LUT bits [23:16] -> |C_X| = 1: X counts terms
  G_SIN           = 3                     ' LUT bits [31:24] -> |C_Y| = 3 (corroborating)
  Y_RATIO         = G_SIN / G_COS         ' every Y reading = 3 x its X reading
  LUTV            = (G_SIN << 24) | (G_COS << 16)       ' $0301_0000
  LUT_LAST        = $1FF                  ' LUT addresses 0..$1FF
  LUT_LONGS       = LUT_LAST + 1

  MODE_S1         = $F007_0000            ' Goertzel SINC1, DACs off, pin group 0
  MODE_S2         = $F087_0000            ' the same with D[23] = 1: SINC2
  SINC2_BIT       = $0080_0000            ' D[23]
  COUNT_MASK      = $0000_FFFF            ' D[15:0]: NCO rollovers per command
  IMM_K           = $0000_8000            ' S[15]=1 sum P3; S[19]=0; S[11:0]=0 (512 loop)
  IMM_Z           = $0000_0000            ' S[15:12]=0 -> every term zero
  ZCOUNT          = 4                     ' zero-burst length (rollovers at F = 1:1)
  N_CAL           = 64                    ' calibration burst length

  FREQ_1TO1       = $8000_0000            ' one rollover per clock (CAL, zero bursts)
  FREQ_P2         = $0080_0000            ' 2^23: exactly 256 clocks per NCO cycle
  FREQ_NPS        = $0080_0040            ' 2^23 + 64: an occasional 255-clock cycle
  FREQ_NPL        = $007F_FFC0            ' 2^23 - 64: an occasional 257-clock cycle
  FREQ_CHIP       = $00A3_D70C            ' 1,000,000.19 Hz at 200 MHz (~200 clk/cycle)
  P2_CYCLE_CLKS   = 256
  CYC_FAST        = 8                     ' NCO cycles per command (fast arms)
  CYC_CHIP        = 100                   ' Chip's 100-cycle measurement
  CYC_LONG        = 25_000                ' ~25 ms per measurement (beyond 20 ms)
  P2_WINDOW       = P2_CYCLE_CLKS * CYC_FAST            ' 2048 clocks
  JIT_MASK        = 1                     ' WAITX #1 WC -> 2 + (1 AND RND) clocks

  NS_FAST         = 1024                  ' samples per fast arm (10.5 ms)
  NS_CHIP         = 2048                  ' samples per CHP arm (204.8 ms)
  NS_LONG         = 16                    ' samples per 25 ms arm (400 ms)
  NS_MAX          = NS_CHIP
  ' 9 fast arms, 3 CHP arms, 2 long arms (see the arm table)
  TOTAL_SAMPLES   = 9 * NS_FAST + 3 * NS_CHIP + 2 * NS_LONG

  WAIT_IDLE       = 500                   ' clocks: > any zero/CAL burst + 16
  WAIT_PIN        = 10_000                ' settle after changing P3
  MBOX_DONE       = 1                     ' mbox[MB_DONE] sentinel: engine finished
  RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC = 5                     ' host wait cap; engine needs ~1.6 s

CON ' ---- Arms, Loop Kinds and Mailbox Layout ----
  ' read-loop kinds:
  '  KIND_XCONT  - XCONT, fixed WAITX #1 before GETXACC
  '  KIND_JITTER - XCONT, WAITX #1 WC before GETXACC (Chip's 1-clock jitter)
  '  KIND_XZERO  - XZERO, fixed WAITX #1 before GETXACC
  #0, KIND_XCONT, KIND_JITTER, KIND_XZERO

  ' arms, in run order (the table in the engine DAT has one row per arm):
  '  ARM_P2_S1 .. ARM_XCL_S2 - see the ARMS table in the header; NARMS = 14
  #0, ARM_P2_S1, ARM_P2_S2, ARM_NPS_S1, ARM_NPS_S2, ARM_NPL_S1, ARM_NPL_S2, ARM_CHP_S1, ARM_CHP_S2, ARM_JIT_S1, ARM_JIT_S2, ARM_XZS_S2, ARM_XZC_S2, ARM_XZL_S2, ARM_XCL_S2, NARMS

  ' arm-table fields:
  '  AF_FREQ - SETXFRQ value   AF_CMD - streamer D (mode | count)
  '  AF_KIND - read-loop kind  AF_NS  - samples recorded
  #0, AF_FREQ, AF_CMD, AF_KIND, AF_NS, ARM_FIELDS

  ' mailbox header longs
  MB_DONE         = 0
  MB_LUTBAD       = 1
  MB_CAL          = 4
  HDR             = 16
  ' calibration record, one per P3 level:
  '  CR_PIN - TESTP level  CR_B/CR_BY - X/Y before  CR_R/CR_RY - X/Y after
  #0, CR_PIN, CR_B, CR_BY, CR_R, CR_RY, CAL_REC
  ' arm header:
  '  AH_CT0 - CT just before XINIT  AH_PINB/AH_PINA - P3 at start/end
  '  AH_NS  - sample count echoed by the engine
  #0, AH_CT0, AH_PINB, AH_PINA, AH_NS, ARM_HDR
  ' sample record:
  '  SR_X - GETXACC X  SR_Y - GETXACC Y  SR_CT - GETCT 4 clocks after it
  #0, SR_X, SR_Y, SR_CT, REC
  MBOX_LONGS      = HDR + NARMS * ARM_HDR + REC * TOTAL_SAMPLES

  ' P3 levels
  LEVEL_LOW       = 0
  LEVEL_HIGH      = 1

  ' model-fit states:
  '  FIT_NONE - not attempted (x at k = WARM would exceed 31 bits)
  '  FIT_OK   - exact fit       FIT_FAIL - the division was not exact
  #0, FIT_NONE, FIT_OK, FIT_FAIL

  ' analysis
  WARM            = 3                     ' first analysed sample (start-up excluded)
  G_MAX           = 2                     ' |g| allowed by the LOCK control
  SPREAD_STEADY   = 1                     ' window max - min allowed, non-jitter arms
  SPREAD_JITTER   = 2                     ' ... jitter arms (D-1 .. D+1)
  HUGE_TERMS      = 1000                  ' Q3: |e| >= 1000 terms is "huge"
  JIT_CONFIRM_PCT = 25
  JIT_REFUTE_PCT  = 5
  PCT             = 100
  X100            = 100                   ' fixed-point scale for periods
  JIT_PRINT       = 48                    ' jitter arms: rows printed
  RAW_PRINT       = 6                     ' raw rows printed per arm
  MIN_RUNS        = 2                     ' Q1: complete runs needed per arm
  MIN_OUT_Q5      = 16                    ' Q5: outliers needed across decisive arms
  PAIR_LEN        = 2
  ONE_CLOCK       = 1                     ' a window one clock longer or shorter
  Q4_PAIRS        = 3                     ' XZERO arms, each with an XCONT twin
  NCO_HALF        = $4000_0000            ' 2^30: (2*M) * 2^30 = M * 2^31, both positive
  NO_INDEX        = -1

VAR ' ---- Mailbox & Analysis State ----
  long mbox[MBOX_LONGS]                   ' engine output (see the layout CONs)
  long modelX[NS_MAX]                     ' model x^ per sample, current SINC2 arm
  long modelXterm[NS_MAX]                  ' model J per sample, current SINC2 arm
  long armBase[NARMS]                     ' mbox index of each arm header
  long armOk[NARMS]                       ' window-spread control passed
  long normLen[NARMS], lenMin[NARMS], lenMax[NARMS]
  long nOddWin[NARMS], firstOddK[NARMS], lastOddK[NARMS]
  long nDsamp[NARMS], nOut[NARMS], nHuge[NARMS], maxAbsErr[NARMS], nDvar[NARMS]
  long nRuns[NARMS], nPairs[NARMS], nEdge[NARMS], nOpen[NARMS]
  long nUnlinked[NARMS], nMissed[NARMS], nChanged[NARMS]
  long nAcctBad[NARMS], nDev1[NARMS], maxDev1[NARMS]
  long fitState[NARMS], fitXterm[NARMS]
  long nMisClean[NARMS], nMisOut[NARMS], firstMisK[NARMS]
  long nYbad[NARMS]
  long calCx, calCy                       ' measured per-clock terms, P3 HIGH
  long gapClocks                          ' g: clocks per window adding no term
  long nRigFail


PUB main() | engineCog, tstart
'' Run the rig: start the measuring engine cog, wait for its done flag, then
'' print the raw data, the controls, the analysis and the five verdicts.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local engineCog - cog the measuring engine runs in
' @local tstart - CT when the wait for the engine began

  longfill(@mbox, 0, MBOX_LONGS)
  debug("=== Goertzel SINC2 iteration-count corruption: reproduce, measure, explain ===")
  print_predictions()
  engineCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @engine, @mbox)
  if engineCog < 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: no free cog for the measuring engine")
    finish()
  tstart := getct()
  repeat until mbox[MB_DONE] == MBOX_DONE or (getct() - tstart) > clkfreq * RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC
  if mbox[MB_DONE] <> MBOX_DONE
    cogstop(engineCog)
    debug("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not report done within 5 s (expected ~1.6 s)")
    finish()
  debug("measuring cog = ", udec_(engineCog), " (debugger restricted to cog 0)")
  report()
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when END_SESSION or
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  debug("=== END ===")
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat


' ------------------------------------------------------------ accessors --
PRI arm_field(armIdx, fieldOff) : fieldVal
' Read one field of the arm table (the engine's own DAT copy, in hub).
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param fieldOff - an AF_xxx field offset
' @returns fieldVal - the table value

  fieldVal := long[@arm_tab][armIdx * ARM_FIELDS + fieldOff]


PRI smp(armIdx, sampIdx, fieldOff) : smpVal
' Read one field of one recorded sample.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param sampIdx - sample index within the arm
' @param fieldOff - an SR_xxx field offset
' @returns smpVal - the recorded value

  smpVal := mbox[armBase[armIdx] + ARM_HDR + sampIdx * REC + fieldOff]


PRI win_len(armIdx, sampIdx) : winClks
' Clocks between read sampIdx-1 and read sampIdx (both GETCTs sit the same
' fixed distance after their GETXACC).
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param sampIdx - sample index within the arm (>= 1)
' @returns winClks - the read-to-read window in clocks

  winClks := smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_CT) - smp(armIdx, sampIdx - 1, SR_CT)


PRI is_sinc2(armIdx) : bSinc2
' Whether the arm's mode word selects SINC2 (D[23] = 1).
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @returns bSinc2 - TRUE for SINC2, FALSE for SINC1

  bSinc2 := (arm_field(armIdx, AF_CMD) & SINC2_BIT) <> 0


PRI arm_name(armIdx) : pName
' Printable arm label.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @returns pName - address of the zero-terminated label

  pName := lookupz(armIdx : @nm_p2s1, @nm_p2s2, @nm_nps1, @nm_nps2, @nm_npl1, @nm_npl2, @nm_chp1, @nm_chp2, @nm_jit1, @nm_jit2, @nm_xzs2, @nm_xzc2, @nm_xzl2, @nm_xcl2)


PRI tri(nTerms) : triSum
' nTerms*(nTerms-1)/2 with the halving done before the multiply, so the
' 32-bit product wraps exactly as the hardware register would.
'
' @param nTerms - number of active clocks in a window (> 0)
' @returns triSum - 0 + 1 + ... + (nTerms-1), mod 2^32

  if nTerms & 1
    triSum := nTerms * ((nTerms - 1) >> 1)
  else
    triSum := (nTerms >> 1) * (nTerms - 1)


PRI pred_windows(freqVal, cycles) : normClk, oddClk, periodX100, zeroClk | quo, remd
' XCONT window prediction from SETXFRQ and the count: the mean command length
' is cycles*2^31/freqVal clocks, so commands take quo or quo+1 clocks.
'
' @param freqVal - SETXFRQ value (positive, < 2^31)
' @param cycles - NCO rollovers per command (D[15:0])
' @returns normClk - the usual XCONT window
' @returns oddClk - the occasional window (= normClk when it never varies)
' @returns periodX100 - commands between odd windows, x100 (0 = never)
' @returns zeroClk - XZERO window, ceil(cycles*2^31/freqVal)

' Local Variables:
' @local quo - floor(cycles*2^31/freqVal)
' @local remd - cycles*2^31 - quo*freqVal (exact: it is < freqVal)

  quo := muldiv64(cycles * 2, NCO_HALF, freqVal)        ' both operands positive
  remd := cycles * FREQ_1TO1 - quo * freqVal            ' low 32 bits are exact
  normClk := quo
  oddClk := quo
  periodX100 := 0
  zeroClk := quo
  if remd <> 0
    zeroClk := quo + 1
    if remd < freqVal - remd
      oddClk := quo + 1
      periodX100 := muldiv64(freqVal, X100, remd)
    else
      normClk := quo + 1
      periodX100 := muldiv64(freqVal, X100, freqVal - remd)


PRI pair_consts(nWin, deltaLen) : constFirst, constNext
' The J-free parts of the carry model's pair errors for C = +G_COS:
' e_k = dl*J + constFirst, e_(k+1) = -dl*J + constNext.
'
' @param nWin - the usual window n (active clocks)
' @param deltaLen - dl, the odd window's length minus n (+1 or -1)
' @returns constFirst - 2*C*n*dl + C*(dl^2-dl)/2
' @returns constNext - -dl*n*C - C*(dl^2-dl)/2

  constFirst := 2 * G_COS * nWin * deltaLen + G_COS * (deltaLen * deltaLen - deltaLen) / 2
  constNext := -deltaLen * nWin * G_COS - G_COS * (deltaLen * deltaLen - deltaLen) / 2


' ---------------------------------------------------------- predictions --
PRI print_predictions() | armIdx, normClk, oddClk, perX100, zeroClk, perUs, constFirst, constNext
' Print the model and every arm's predicted windows and pair errors, all
' computed from the arm table before any measured value is read.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local normClk - predicted usual XCONT window
' @local oddClk - predicted odd XCONT window
' @local perX100 - predicted odd-window period, commands x100
' @local zeroClk - predicted XZERO window
' @local perUs - predicted odd-window period, microseconds
' @local constFirst - J-free part of the predicted e_k
' @local constNext - J-free part of the predicted e_(k+1)

  debug("PREDICTIONS (fixed before the run):")
  debug("  term per active clock: C_X = +1, C_Y = +3 with P3 HIGH (LUT $0301_0000, S = $0000_8000)")
  debug("  carry model: SINC1 xterm := C | SINC2 xterm := xterm + C | xsum += xterm before the edge (EF-070)")
  debug("  GETXACC mid-stream returns xsum and zeroes it, exact partition (EF-069); xterm is not cleared")
  debug("  window k: n_k active clocks, J_k = xterm added on its first clock:")
  debug("    x_k = n_k*J_k + C*n_k*(n_k-1)/2    J_(k+1) = J_k + C*n_k    d_k = x_k - x_(k-1)")
  debug("    equal windows n: d = C*n^2 | one window n+dl between windows n:")
  debug("    e_k = dl*J_(k-1) + 2*C*n*dl + C*(dl^2-dl)/2   e_(k+1) = -dl*J_(k-1) - dl*n*C - C*(dl^2-dl)/2   e_(k+2) = 0")
  debug("    SINC1: x_k = C*n_k -> the odd window reads exactly dl*C off, alone")
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    normClk, oddClk, perX100, zeroClk := pred_windows(arm_field(armIdx, AF_FREQ), arm_field(armIdx, AF_CMD) & COUNT_MASK)
    perUs := muldiv64(perX100, normClk, CLK_MHZ * X100)
    debug("  ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), ": F=", uhex_long_(arm_field(armIdx, AF_FREQ)), " M=", udec_(arm_field(armIdx, AF_CMD) & COUNT_MASK), " | XCONT windows ", udec_(normClk), ", odd ", udec_(oddClk), " every x100 = ", udec_(perX100), " cmds (", udec_(perUs), " us) | XZERO window ", udec_(zeroClk))
    if oddClk <> normClk and is_sinc2(armIdx) and arm_field(armIdx, AF_KIND) == KIND_XCONT
      constFirst, constNext := pair_consts(normClk, oddClk - normClk)
      debug("    SINC2 pair (C=+1): d0 = ", sdec_(G_COS * normClk * normClk), ", e_k = ", sdec_(oddClk - normClk), "*J + ", sdec_(constFirst), ", e_(k+1) = ", sdec_(normClk - oddClk), "*J + ", sdec_(constNext), ", sum = ", sdec_(constFirst + constNext))
  debug("  Q3: JIT windows 2047/2048/2049; SINC2 corrupted where n_k <> n_(k-1) (~75 %), |e| ~ J >> 1000; SINC1 +-1 term (~50 %)")
  debug("  Q4: each XZERO arm keeps one window length and shows 0 outliers")
  debug("  Q5: every x_k equals the model x^_k (fit once at k = 3), clean rows and outliers alike")


' --------------------------------------------------------------- report --
PRI report() | armIdx, bGo
' Run the controls in order; if every one passed, analyse every arm and print
' the verdicts, else print the raw head of every arm and withhold verdicts.

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local bGo - TRUE while every control upstream has passed

  nRigFail := 0
  locate_arms()
  check_lut()
  check_cal()
  check_pins()
  bGo := (nRigFail == 0)
  if bGo
    check_lock()
    bGo := (nRigFail == 0)
  if bGo
    debug("controls: LUT ok, CAL ok (C sign flips with P3, C_Y = 3*C_X), pins ok, loop locked, g ok, sizes ok")
    repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
      analyze_arm(armIdx)
    verdicts()
  else
    repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
      print_raw_head(armIdx)
    debug("NO VERDICT: a rig control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above)")


' ------------------------------------------------------------- controls --
PRI locate_arms() | armIdx, offs
' Compute each arm's mailbox offset by walking the table the engine walks,
' and check the total against the mailbox size.

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local offs - running mailbox index

  offs := HDR
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    armBase[armIdx] := offs
    offs += ARM_HDR + REC * arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
  if offs <> MBOX_LONGS
    debug("RIG FAIL: arm table needs ", udec_(offs), " mailbox longs, mailbox has ", udec_(MBOX_LONGS))
    nRigFail++


PRI check_lut()
' LUT control: the engine read all 512 LUT longs back after writing them.
'

  debug("LUT readback: ", udec_(mbox[MB_LUTBAD]), " of ", udec_(LUT_LONGS), " longs differ from ", uhex_long_(LUTV))
  if mbox[MB_LUTBAD] <> 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: LUT readback, expected 0 mismatches, got ", udec_(mbox[MB_LUTBAD]))
    nRigFail++


PRI check_cal() | lvl, calBase, deltaX, deltaY, cxLvl[2], cyLvl[2], nBad
' CAL control: R - B = N_CAL * C on both channels at both P3 levels; |C_X| =
' G_COS, C_Y = Y_RATIO * C_X, and C flips sign with P3.

' Local Variables:
' @local lvl - P3 level
' @local calBase - mailbox index of the level's record
' @local deltaX - X: R - B
' @local deltaY - Y: R - B
' @local cxLvl - measured C_X per level
' @local cyLvl - measured C_Y per level
' @local nBad - control failures found

  nBad := 0
  repeat lvl from LEVEL_LOW to LEVEL_HIGH
    calBase := MB_CAL + lvl * CAL_REC
    deltaX := mbox[calBase + CR_R] - mbox[calBase + CR_B]
    deltaY := mbox[calBase + CR_RY] - mbox[calBase + CR_BY]
    debug("CAL P3 set ", udec_(lvl), " read ", udec_(mbox[calBase + CR_PIN]), ": X B=", sdec_(mbox[calBase + CR_B]), " R=", sdec_(mbox[calBase + CR_R]), " R-B=", sdec_(deltaX), " | Y B=", sdec_(mbox[calBase + CR_BY]), " R=", sdec_(mbox[calBase + CR_RY]), " R-B=", sdec_(deltaY))
    cxLvl[lvl] := 0
    cyLvl[lvl] := 0
    if mbox[calBase + CR_PIN] <> lvl
      debug("RIG FAIL: CAL pin, expected P3 = ", udec_(lvl), ", got ", udec_(mbox[calBase + CR_PIN]))
      nBad++
    if (deltaX // N_CAL) <> 0 or (deltaY // N_CAL) <> 0
      debug("RIG FAIL: CAL deltas not whole multiples of ", udec_(N_CAL), " at P3 = ", udec_(lvl))
      nBad++
    else
      cxLvl[lvl] := deltaX / N_CAL
      cyLvl[lvl] := deltaY / N_CAL
      if abs cxLvl[lvl] <> G_COS or cyLvl[lvl] <> Y_RATIO * cxLvl[lvl]
        debug("RIG FAIL: CAL term at P3 = ", udec_(lvl), ": C_X = ", sdec_(cxLvl[lvl]), " C_Y = ", sdec_(cyLvl[lvl]), " (expected |C_X| = 1, C_Y = 3*C_X)")
        nBad++
  if cxLvl[LEVEL_LOW] <> -cxLvl[LEVEL_HIGH] or cxLvl[LEVEL_HIGH] == 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: CAL sign did not flip with P3: C_X(LOW) = ", sdec_(cxLvl[LEVEL_LOW]), " C_X(HIGH) = ", sdec_(cxLvl[LEVEL_HIGH]))
    nBad++
  calCx := cxLvl[LEVEL_HIGH]
  calCy := cyLvl[LEVEL_HIGH]
  debug("C measured: X LOW ", sdec_(cxLvl[LEVEL_LOW]), " HIGH ", sdec_(cxLvl[LEVEL_HIGH]), " | Y LOW ", sdec_(cyLvl[LEVEL_LOW]), " HIGH ", sdec_(cyLvl[LEVEL_HIGH]), "  (predicted -1 / +1, -3 / +3); the arms use the HIGH values")
  nRigFail += nBad


PRI check_pins() | armIdx, nBad
' PIN and SIZE controls: P3 HIGH at every arm's start and end, and the
' engine's sample-count echo equals the table.

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local nBad - control failures found

  nBad := 0
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    if mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_PINB] <> LEVEL_HIGH or mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_PINA] <> LEVEL_HIGH
      debug("RIG FAIL: pin control, ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), " P3 start/end = ", udec_(mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_PINB]), "/", udec_(mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_PINA]), " (expected 1/1)")
      nBad++
    if mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_NS] <> arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
      debug("RIG FAIL: size control, ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), " engine echoed ", udec_(mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_NS]), " samples, table has ", udec_(arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)))
      nBad++
  nRigFail += nBad


PRI check_lock() | sampIdx, nsArm, xRef, nBadWin1, nBadWin2, nBadX
' LOCK control: in both power-of-two arms every window is exactly 2048 clocks
' (reads locked to command boundaries); in P2-S1 every x is equal and whole
' in C, which measures g.

' Local Variables:
' @local sampIdx - sample index
' @local nsArm - samples in the arm
' @local xRef - P2-S1 x at k = WARM
' @local nBadWin1 - P2-S1 windows <> 2048
' @local nBadWin2 - P2-S2 windows <> 2048
' @local nBadX - P2-S1 samples <> xRef

  nsArm := arm_field(ARM_P2_S1, AF_NS)
  xRef := smp(ARM_P2_S1, WARM, SR_X)
  nBadWin1 := 0
  nBadWin2 := 0
  nBadX := 0
  repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
    if win_len(ARM_P2_S1, sampIdx) <> P2_WINDOW
      nBadWin1++
    if win_len(ARM_P2_S2, sampIdx) <> P2_WINDOW
      nBadWin2++
    if smp(ARM_P2_S1, sampIdx, SR_X) <> xRef
      nBadX++
  debug("LOCK: P2-S1 windows <> ", udec_(P2_WINDOW), ": ", udec_(nBadWin1), ", P2-S2: ", udec_(nBadWin2), " (of ", udec_(nsArm - WARM), " each); P2-S1 x <> ", sdec_(xRef), ": ", udec_(nBadX))
  gapClocks := 0
  if nBadWin1 or nBadWin2 or nBadX
    debug("RIG FAIL: LOCK, the power-of-two stream is not perfectly steady (expected 0 / 0 / 0)")
    nRigFail++
  elseif (xRef // calCx) <> 0
    debug("RIG FAIL: LOCK, P2-S1 x = ", sdec_(xRef), " is not a whole multiple of C = ", sdec_(calCx))
    nRigFail++
  else
    gapClocks := P2_WINDOW - xRef / calCx
    debug("  g = 2048 - x/C = ", sdec_(gapClocks), " clocks per window adding no term (seamless XCONT: expected 0)")
    if abs gapClocks > G_MAX
      debug("RIG FAIL: LOCK, |g| = ", udec_(abs gapClocks), " exceeds ", udec_(G_MAX))
      nRigFail++


' ------------------------------------------------------------- per arm --
PRI analyze_arm(armIdx)
' Window statistics, the raw head, then the SINC1 or SINC2 analysis and the
' Y corroboration for one arm.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

  debug(" ")
  arm_windows(armIdx)
  print_raw_head(armIdx)
  if is_sinc2(armIdx)
    analyze_sinc2(armIdx)
  else
    analyze_sinc1(armIdx)
  check_y(armIdx)


PRI arm_windows(armIdx) | nsArm, sampIdx, winClks, cntAt0, cntAt1, cntAt2, maxSpread, normClk, oddClk, perX100, zeroClk, spacingX100
' Window-length histogram, usual window, odd windows and their spacing, the
' predicted values beside them, and the SPREAD control for one arm.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

' Local Variables:
' @local nsArm - samples in the arm
' @local sampIdx - sample index
' @local winClks - one window length
' @local cntAt0 - windows of length min
' @local cntAt1 - windows of length min+1
' @local cntAt2 - windows of length min+2
' @local maxSpread - SPREAD limit for this arm
' @local normClk - predicted usual window
' @local oddClk - predicted odd window
' @local perX100 - predicted odd-window period, commands x100
' @local zeroClk - predicted XZERO window
' @local spacingX100 - measured odd-window spacing, samples x100

  nsArm := arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
  lenMin[armIdx] := POSX
  lenMax[armIdx] := NEGX
  cntAt0 := 0
  cntAt1 := 0
  cntAt2 := 0
  repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
    winClks := win_len(armIdx, sampIdx)
    lenMin[armIdx] := lenMin[armIdx] <# winClks
    lenMax[armIdx] := lenMax[armIdx] #> winClks
  repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
    case win_len(armIdx, sampIdx) - lenMin[armIdx]
      0: cntAt0++
      1: cntAt1++
      2: cntAt2++
  normLen[armIdx] := lenMin[armIdx]
  if cntAt1 > cntAt0 and cntAt1 >= cntAt2
    normLen[armIdx] := lenMin[armIdx] + 1
  elseif cntAt2 > cntAt0 and cntAt2 > cntAt1
    normLen[armIdx] := lenMin[armIdx] + 2
  nOddWin[armIdx] := 0
  firstOddK[armIdx] := NO_INDEX
  lastOddK[armIdx] := NO_INDEX
  repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
    if win_len(armIdx, sampIdx) <> normLen[armIdx]
      nOddWin[armIdx]++
      if firstOddK[armIdx] == NO_INDEX
        firstOddK[armIdx] := sampIdx
      lastOddK[armIdx] := sampIdx
  maxSpread := SPREAD_STEADY
  if arm_field(armIdx, AF_KIND) == KIND_JITTER
    maxSpread := SPREAD_JITTER
  armOk[armIdx] := (lenMax[armIdx] - lenMin[armIdx]) <= maxSpread
  normClk, oddClk, perX100, zeroClk := pred_windows(arm_field(armIdx, AF_FREQ), arm_field(armIdx, AF_CMD) & COUNT_MASK)
  spacingX100 := 0
  if nOddWin[armIdx] > 1
    spacingX100 := (lastOddK[armIdx] - firstOddK[armIdx]) * X100 / (nOddWin[armIdx] - 1)
  debug("=== ARM ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), "  F=", uhex_long_(arm_field(armIdx, AF_FREQ)), " D=", uhex_long_(arm_field(armIdx, AF_CMD)), " samples ", udec_(nsArm), " ===")
  debug("  windows k>=3: min ", udec_(lenMin[armIdx]), " x", udec_(cntAt0), ", min+1 x", udec_(cntAt1), ", min+2 x", udec_(cntAt2), "; usual ", udec_(normLen[armIdx]), "; odd windows ", udec_(nOddWin[armIdx]), " (first k=", sdec_(firstOddK[armIdx]), ", last k=", sdec_(lastOddK[armIdx]), ")")
  debug("  measured odd spacing x100 = ", udec_(spacingX100), " samples (", udec_(muldiv64(spacingX100, normLen[armIdx], CLK_MHZ * X100)), " us) | predicted XCONT ", udec_(normClk), "/", udec_(oddClk), " every x100 = ", udec_(perX100), " cmds, XZERO ", udec_(zeroClk))
  if not armOk[armIdx]
    debug("RIG FAIL (arm ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), "): window spread ", udec_(lenMax[armIdx] - lenMin[armIdx]), " clocks, allowed ", udec_(maxSpread), " -- the loop is not locked to command boundaries; verdicts using this arm are withheld")


PRI print_raw_head(armIdx) | sampIdx
' Print the first RAW_PRINT raw samples of one arm (start-up included).
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

' Local Variables:
' @local sampIdx - sample index

  debug("  raw ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), " CT at XINIT = ", uhex_long_(mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_CT0]))
  repeat sampIdx from 0 to RAW_PRINT - 1
    if sampIdx == 0
      debug("  raw k=0 x=", sdec_(smp(armIdx, 0, SR_X)), " y=", sdec_(smp(armIdx, 0, SR_Y)), " ct-ct0=", sdec_(smp(armIdx, 0, SR_CT) - mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_CT0]))
    else
      debug("  raw k=", udec_(sampIdx), " x=", sdec_(smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X)), " y=", sdec_(smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_Y)), " L=", udec_(win_len(armIdx, sampIdx)), " d=", sdec_(smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X) - smp(armIdx, sampIdx - 1, SR_X)))


PRI analyze_sinc1(armIdx) | nsArm, sampIdx, winClks, xVal, predVal, devVal, printLimit
' SINC1 accounting (Q2, Q3): every sample must equal C*(L_k - g); the
' deviation from the usual sample is counted and its largest size kept.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

' Local Variables:
' @local nsArm - samples in the arm
' @local sampIdx - sample index
' @local winClks - window length
' @local xVal - measured x
' @local predVal - C*(L - g)
' @local devVal - x - C*(usual - g)
' @local printLimit - rows past this index are not printed (jitter arm)

  nsArm := arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
  nAcctBad[armIdx] := 0
  nDev1[armIdx] := 0
  maxDev1[armIdx] := 0
  printLimit := nsArm
  if arm_field(armIdx, AF_KIND) == KIND_JITTER
    printLimit := WARM + JIT_PRINT
  debug("  SINC1 rows (odd windows; jitter arm: first rows only; any x <> C*(L-g) always):")
  repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
    winClks := win_len(armIdx, sampIdx)
    xVal := smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X)
    predVal := calCx * (winClks - gapClocks)
    devVal := xVal - calCx * (normLen[armIdx] - gapClocks)
    if xVal <> predVal
      nAcctBad[armIdx]++
    if devVal <> 0
      nDev1[armIdx]++
    maxDev1[armIdx] := maxDev1[armIdx] #> abs devVal
    if xVal <> predVal or (winClks <> normLen[armIdx] and sampIdx < printLimit)
      debug("  k=", udec_(sampIdx), " L=", udec_(winClks), " x=", sdec_(xVal), " x-C*(L-g)=", sdec_(xVal - predVal), " dev=x-x_usual=", sdec_(devVal))
  debug("  SINC1: ", udec_(nsArm - WARM), " samples; x <> C*(L-g) in ", udec_(nAcctBad[armIdx]), "; off the usual value in ", udec_(nDev1[armIdx]), "; max |dev| = ", udec_(maxDev1[armIdx]), " (one term = ", udec_(abs calCx), ", usual x = ", sdec_(calCx * (normLen[armIdx] - gapClocks)), ")")


PRI fit_model(armIdx) | nsArm, clocksToFit, nWin, numer, xtermRun, sampIdx, nWinK
' Fit J once at k = WARM (exact division required), then fill the model x^ and
' J for every later sample from the measured windows alone.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

' Local Variables:
' @local nsArm - samples in the arm
' @local clocksToFit - clocks from the arm's XINIT to read WARM-1
' @local nWin - active clocks in window WARM
' @local numer - x_WARM - C*tri(nWin)
' @local xtermRun - running model J
' @local sampIdx - sample index
' @local nWinK - active clocks in window k

  nsArm := arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
  fitState[armIdx] := FIT_NONE
  fitXterm[armIdx] := 0
  nWin := win_len(armIdx, WARM) - gapClocks
  clocksToFit := smp(armIdx, WARM - 1, SR_CT) - mbox[armBase[armIdx] + AH_CT0]
  numer := 0
  if (clocksToFit + nWin) < (POSX / nWin) / abs calCx
    numer := smp(armIdx, WARM, SR_X) - calCx * tri(nWin)
    if (numer // nWin) == 0
      fitState[armIdx] := FIT_OK
      fitXterm[armIdx] := numer / nWin
    else
      fitState[armIdx] := FIT_FAIL
  if fitState[armIdx] == FIT_OK
    xtermRun := fitXterm[armIdx]
    repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
      nWinK := win_len(armIdx, sampIdx) - gapClocks
      modelXterm[sampIdx] := xtermRun
      modelX[sampIdx] := nWinK * xtermRun + calCx * tri(nWinK)
      xtermRun += calCx * nWinK
    debug("  model fit at k=3: J = (x - C*n(n-1)/2)/n = ", sdec_(fitXterm[armIdx]), " = ", sdec_(fitXterm[armIdx] / calCx), " terms; clocks XINIT -> read 2 = ", udec_(clocksToFit), " (J/C - clocks = ", sdec_(fitXterm[armIdx] / calCx - clocksToFit), ": start offset)")
  elseif fitState[armIdx] == FIT_FAIL
    debug("  model fit FAILED at k=3: x - C*n(n-1)/2 = ", sdec_(numer), " is not a multiple of n = ", udec_(nWin))
  else
    debug("  model fit skipped: n*J would pass 31 bits at k=3 (window ", udec_(nWin), " clocks); constant-window checks only")


PRI analyze_sinc2(armIdx) | nsArm, kindVal, nNorm, dClean, dFirst, sampIdx, dVal, errVal, bOut, bChanged, bMis, runStart, printLimit
' SINC2 analysis (Q1, Q3, Q4, Q5): classify every difference sample against
' C*n^2 and against the window rule, count how many differ from the first
' analysed sample, compare every x with the model, group outliers into runs,
' and print every outlier with its neighbours.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

' Local Variables:
' @local nsArm - samples in the arm
' @local kindVal - read-loop kind
' @local nNorm - usual active clocks per window
' @local dClean - C*n^2, the clean SINC2 sample
' @local dFirst - d at k = WARM+1, the reference for constancy (Q4)
' @local sampIdx - sample index
' @local dVal - d_k = x_k - x_(k-1)
' @local errVal - d_k - dClean
' @local bOut - d_k <> dClean
' @local bChanged - n_k or n_(k-1) differs from the usual window
' @local bMis - x_k <> model x^_k
' @local runStart - first sample of the open outlier run, or NO_INDEX
' @local printLimit - rows past this index are not printed (jitter arm)

  nsArm := arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
  kindVal := arm_field(armIdx, AF_KIND)
  nNorm := normLen[armIdx] - gapClocks
  dClean := calCx * nNorm * nNorm
  fit_model(armIdx)
  nDsamp[armIdx] := 0
  nOut[armIdx] := 0
  nHuge[armIdx] := 0
  maxAbsErr[armIdx] := 0
  nDvar[armIdx] := 0
  dFirst := smp(armIdx, WARM + 1, SR_X) - smp(armIdx, WARM, SR_X)
  nRuns[armIdx] := 0
  nPairs[armIdx] := 0
  nEdge[armIdx] := 0
  nOpen[armIdx] := 0
  nUnlinked[armIdx] := 0
  nMissed[armIdx] := 0
  nChanged[armIdx] := 0
  nMisClean[armIdx] := 0
  nMisOut[armIdx] := 0
  firstMisK[armIdx] := NO_INDEX
  printLimit := nsArm
  if kindVal == KIND_JITTER
    printLimit := WARM + JIT_PRINT
  debug("  SINC2: d0 = C*n^2 = ", sdec_(dClean), " (n = ", udec_(nNorm), "); rows: every outlier and its neighbours (jitter arm: first rows), every model mismatch")
  debug("  row: k L x d e=d-d0 | model J x^ e^ -> MATCH/MISMATCH")
  runStart := NO_INDEX
  repeat sampIdx from WARM + 1 to nsArm - 1
    dVal := smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X) - smp(armIdx, sampIdx - 1, SR_X)
    errVal := dVal - dClean
    bOut := (dVal <> dClean)
    bChanged := win_len(armIdx, sampIdx) <> normLen[armIdx] or win_len(armIdx, sampIdx - 1) <> normLen[armIdx]
    bMis := FALSE
    nDsamp[armIdx]++
    if dVal <> dFirst
      nDvar[armIdx]++
    if bChanged
      nChanged[armIdx]++
    if bOut
      nOut[armIdx]++
      maxAbsErr[armIdx] := maxAbsErr[armIdx] #> abs errVal
      if abs errVal >= HUGE_TERMS * abs calCx
        nHuge[armIdx]++
      if not bChanged
        nUnlinked[armIdx]++
    elseif bChanged
      nMissed[armIdx]++
    if fitState[armIdx] == FIT_OK
      if smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X) <> modelX[sampIdx]
        bMis := TRUE
        if firstMisK[armIdx] == NO_INDEX
          firstMisK[armIdx] := sampIdx
        if bChanged
          nMisOut[armIdx]++
        else
          nMisClean[armIdx]++
    if bOut and runStart == NO_INDEX
      runStart := sampIdx
      if kindVal <> KIND_JITTER
        print_pair_formula(armIdx, sampIdx)
    elseif not bOut and runStart <> NO_INDEX
      close_run(armIdx, runStart, sampIdx - runStart, TRUE)
      runStart := NO_INDEX
    if bMis or (sampIdx < printLimit and (bOut or is_out(armIdx, sampIdx - 1, dClean) or is_out(armIdx, sampIdx + 1, dClean)))
      print_s2_row(armIdx, sampIdx, dClean)
  if runStart <> NO_INDEX
    close_run(armIdx, runStart, nsArm - runStart, FALSE)
  debug("  SINC2: ", udec_(nDsamp[armIdx]), " samples; outliers ", udec_(nOut[armIdx]), " (huge >= 1000 terms: ", udec_(nHuge[armIdx]), ", max |e| ", udec_(maxAbsErr[armIdx]), "); window-changed samples ", udec_(nChanged[armIdx]), ", of them clean ", udec_(nMissed[armIdx]), "; outliers with no window change ", udec_(nUnlinked[armIdx]))
  debug("  runs ", udec_(nRuns[armIdx]), ": pairs ", udec_(nPairs[armIdx]), ", start-edge ", udec_(nEdge[armIdx]), ", open at end ", udec_(nOpen[armIdx]), " | model mismatches: clean-window ", udec_(nMisClean[armIdx]), ", window-changed ", udec_(nMisOut[armIdx]), " (first k=", sdec_(firstMisK[armIdx]), ")")
  debug("  constancy: d differs from d(k=4) = ", sdec_(dFirst), " in ", udec_(nDvar[armIdx]), " samples")


PRI is_out(armIdx, sampIdx, dClean) : bOutlier
' Whether sample sampIdx is an analysed SINC2 outlier (d_k <> dClean).
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param sampIdx - sample index (outside WARM+1..ns-1 -> FALSE)
' @param dClean - C*n^2, the clean SINC2 sample
' @returns bOutlier - TRUE when d_k <> dClean

  bOutlier := FALSE
  if sampIdx > WARM and sampIdx < arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
    bOutlier := (smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X) - smp(armIdx, sampIdx - 1, SR_X)) <> dClean


PRI print_s2_row(armIdx, sampIdx, dClean) | xVal, dVal, dHat
' Print one SINC2 row: measured x, d, e beside the model's J, x^ and e^.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param sampIdx - sample index (> WARM)
' @param dClean - C*n^2, the clean SINC2 sample

' Local Variables:
' @local xVal - measured x_k
' @local dVal - measured d_k
' @local dHat - model d^_k

  xVal := smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X)
  dVal := xVal - smp(armIdx, sampIdx - 1, SR_X)
  if fitState[armIdx] == FIT_OK
    dHat := modelX[sampIdx] - modelX[sampIdx - 1]
    debug("  k=", udec_(sampIdx), " L=", udec_(win_len(armIdx, sampIdx)), " x=", sdec_(xVal), " d=", sdec_(dVal), " e=", sdec_(dVal - dClean), " | J=", sdec_(modelXterm[sampIdx]), " x^=", sdec_(modelX[sampIdx]), " e^=", sdec_(dHat - dClean), " -> ", zstr_(xVal == modelX[sampIdx] ? @s_match : @s_mismatch))
  else
    debug("  k=", udec_(sampIdx), " L=", udec_(win_len(armIdx, sampIdx)), " x=", sdec_(xVal), " d=", sdec_(dVal), " e=", sdec_(dVal - dClean), " | no model")


PRI print_pair_formula(armIdx, sampIdx) | nPrev, nCur, deltaLen, xtermPrev, errFirst, errNext
' At the start of an outlier run, print the closed-form pair prediction
' e_k, e_(k+1) from J_(k-1), valid when the window after the odd one is usual.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param sampIdx - first sample of the run

' Local Variables:
' @local nPrev - active clocks in window k-1
' @local nCur - active clocks in window k
' @local deltaLen - dl = nCur - nPrev
' @local xtermPrev - model J_(k-1)
' @local errFirst - predicted e_k
' @local errNext - predicted e_(k+1)

  nPrev := win_len(armIdx, sampIdx - 1) - gapClocks
  nCur := win_len(armIdx, sampIdx) - gapClocks
  deltaLen := nCur - nPrev
  if fitState[armIdx] == FIT_OK and abs deltaLen == ONE_CLOCK
    xtermPrev := modelXterm[sampIdx - 1]
    errFirst := deltaLen * xtermPrev + 2 * calCx * nPrev * deltaLen + calCx * (deltaLen * deltaLen - deltaLen) / 2
    errNext := -deltaLen * xtermPrev - deltaLen * nPrev * calCx - calCx * (deltaLen * deltaLen - deltaLen) / 2
    debug("  pair formula at k=", udec_(sampIdx), ": dl=", sdec_(deltaLen), " n=", udec_(nPrev), " J_(k-1)=", sdec_(xtermPrev), " -> e_k=", sdec_(errFirst), " e_(k+1)=", sdec_(errNext), " sum=", sdec_(errFirst + errNext), " (if window k+1 is usual)")


PRI close_run(armIdx, runStart, runLen, bClosed)
' Classify one finished outlier run: open at the arm's end, truncated at the
' start edge, an adjacent pair (odd window then a usual one), or other.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @param runStart - first sample of the run
' @param runLen - samples in the run
' @param bClosed - TRUE when a clean sample followed the run

  nRuns[armIdx]++
  if not bClosed
    nOpen[armIdx]++
  elseif runStart == WARM + 1 and win_len(armIdx, WARM) <> normLen[armIdx]
    nEdge[armIdx]++
  elseif runLen == PAIR_LEN and win_len(armIdx, runStart) <> normLen[armIdx] and win_len(armIdx, runStart + 1) == normLen[armIdx]
    nPairs[armIdx]++
  elseif arm_field(armIdx, AF_KIND) <> KIND_JITTER
    debug("  run at k=", udec_(runStart), " length ", udec_(runLen), " is NOT an adjacent pair")


PRI check_y(armIdx) | nsArm, sampIdx, nBad
' Y corroboration (not gating): every analysed y must equal (C_Y/C_X) * x.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1

' Local Variables:
' @local nsArm - samples in the arm
' @local sampIdx - sample index
' @local nBad - samples where y <> ratio * x

  nsArm := arm_field(armIdx, AF_NS)
  nBad := 0
  repeat sampIdx from WARM to nsArm - 1
    if smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_Y) <> (calCy / calCx) * smp(armIdx, sampIdx, SR_X)
      nBad++
  nYbad[armIdx] := nBad
  debug("  Y (corroborating, not gating): y <> ", sdec_(calCy / calCx), "*x in ", udec_(nBad), " of ", udec_(nsArm - WARM), " samples")


' ------------------------------------------------------------- verdicts --
PRI verdicts()
' Print the five verdict lines (each question has its own gating).
'

  debug(" ")
  debug("=== VERDICTS ===")
  verdict_q1()
  verdict_q2()
  verdict_q3()
  verdict_q4()
  verdict_q5()


PRI complete_runs(armIdx) : runCount
' Runs that can be judged: neither truncated at the start nor open at the end.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @returns runCount - nRuns - nEdge - nOpen

  runCount := nRuns[armIdx] - nEdge[armIdx] - nOpen[armIdx]


PRI verdict_q1() | armIdx, bArmsOk, bEnough, bPairsOk, nUnl, nMiss, predNorm, predOdd, predPerX100, predZero
' Q1: non-power-of-two -> adjacent-pair outliers that self-correct; power of
' two -> none.

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local bArmsOk - every Q1 arm passed its SPREAD control
' @local bEnough - every non-power-of-two arm has >= MIN_RUNS complete runs
' @local bPairsOk - every complete run is an adjacent pair
' @local nUnl - outliers with no window change, over the Q1 arms
' @local nMiss - window changes that left d clean, over the Q1 arms
' @local predNorm - CHP predicted usual window
' @local predOdd - CHP predicted odd window
' @local predPerX100 - CHP predicted odd-window period, commands x100
' @local predZero - CHP predicted XZERO window

  bArmsOk := armOk[ARM_P2_S2] and armOk[ARM_NPS_S2] and armOk[ARM_NPL_S2] and armOk[ARM_CHP_S2]
  bEnough := TRUE
  bPairsOk := TRUE
  nUnl := nUnlinked[ARM_P2_S2]
  nMiss := nMissed[ARM_P2_S2]
  repeat armIdx from ARM_NPS_S2 to ARM_CHP_S2 step 2
    debug("Q1 ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), ": outliers ", udec_(nOut[armIdx]), " of ", udec_(nDsamp[armIdx]), " samples, odd windows ", udec_(nOddWin[armIdx]), ", runs ", udec_(nRuns[armIdx]), " (complete ", udec_(complete_runs(armIdx)), ", pairs ", udec_(nPairs[armIdx]), ")")
    nUnl += nUnlinked[armIdx]
    nMiss += nMissed[armIdx]
    if complete_runs(armIdx) < MIN_RUNS
      bEnough := FALSE
    if nPairs[armIdx] <> complete_runs(armIdx)
      bPairsOk := FALSE
  predNorm, predOdd, predPerX100, predZero := pred_windows(arm_field(ARM_CHP_S2, AF_FREQ), arm_field(ARM_CHP_S2, AF_CMD) & COUNT_MASK)
  debug("Q1 cadence, CHP-S2 (1,000,000.19 Hz at 200 MHz, 100-cycle measurements): odd windows every x100 = ", udec_(odd_spacing_x100(ARM_CHP_S2)), " samples = ", udec_(muldiv64(odd_spacing_x100(ARM_CHP_S2), normLen[ARM_CHP_S2], CLK_MHZ * X100)), " us; predicted x100 = ", udec_(predPerX100), " = ", udec_(muldiv64(predPerX100, predNorm, CLK_MHZ * X100)), " us (windows ", udec_(predNorm), "/", udec_(predOdd), ", XZERO ", udec_(predZero), ")")
  if not bArmsOk
    debug("VERDICT Q1: INCONCLUSIVE - a Q1 arm failed its window control (RIG FAIL above)")
  elseif nOut[ARM_P2_S2] <> 0
    debug("VERDICT Q1: REFUTED - the power-of-two SINC2 stream is not clean: ", udec_(nOut[ARM_P2_S2]), " of ", udec_(nDsamp[ARM_P2_S2]), " samples off C*n^2")
  elseif nOut[ARM_NPS_S2] == 0 or nOut[ARM_NPL_S2] == 0
    debug("VERDICT Q1: REFUTED - a varying count left SINC2 clean: NPS-S2 ", udec_(nOut[ARM_NPS_S2]), " outliers (", udec_(nOddWin[ARM_NPS_S2]), " odd windows), NPL-S2 ", udec_(nOut[ARM_NPL_S2]), " (", udec_(nOddWin[ARM_NPL_S2]), ")")
  elseif nUnl <> 0
    debug("VERDICT Q1: INCONCLUSIVE - ", udec_(nUnl), " outlier(s) with no window change: another cause is present")
  elseif nMiss <> 0
    debug("VERDICT Q1: REFUTED - ", udec_(nMiss), " window-changed sample(s) read clean: a varying count does not always corrupt")
  elseif not bEnough
    debug("VERDICT Q1: INCONCLUSIVE - fewer than ", udec_(MIN_RUNS), " complete outlier runs in a non-power-of-two arm")
  elseif not bPairsOk
    debug("VERDICT Q1: REFUTED - outliers are not all adjacent pairs that self-correct (see the run lines above)")
  else
    debug("VERDICT Q1: CONFIRMED - power of two: 0 of ", udec_(nDsamp[ARM_P2_S2]), " off; non-power-of-two: every odd window corrupts that sample and the next, then clean (pairs NPS ", udec_(nPairs[ARM_NPS_S2]), ", NPL ", udec_(nPairs[ARM_NPL_S2]), ", CHP ", udec_(nPairs[ARM_CHP_S2]), "); rates ", udec_(nOut[ARM_NPS_S2]), "/", udec_(nDsamp[ARM_NPS_S2]), ", ", udec_(nOut[ARM_NPL_S2]), "/", udec_(nDsamp[ARM_NPL_S2]), ", ", udec_(nOut[ARM_CHP_S2]), "/", udec_(nDsamp[ARM_CHP_S2]))


PRI odd_spacing_x100(armIdx) : spacingX100
' Mean spacing between odd windows, in samples x100 (0 when fewer than two).
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @returns spacingX100 - mean spacing x100

  spacingX100 := 0
  if nOddWin[armIdx] > 1
    spacingX100 := (lastOddK[armIdx] - firstOddK[armIdx]) * X100 / (nOddWin[armIdx] - 1)


PRI verdict_q2() | armIdx, bArmsOk, bVaried, nAcct, worstDev
' Q2: SINC1 under the same varying counts -- exactly one term off, alone.

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local bArmsOk - every Q2 arm passed its SPREAD control
' @local bVaried - every Q2 arm had odd windows
' @local nAcct - SINC1 samples <> C*(L-g), over the Q2 arms
' @local worstDev - largest |x - x_usual|, over the Q2 arms

  bArmsOk := armOk[ARM_NPS_S1] and armOk[ARM_NPL_S1] and armOk[ARM_CHP_S1]
  bVaried := TRUE
  nAcct := 0
  worstDev := 0
  repeat armIdx from ARM_NPS_S1 to ARM_CHP_S1 step 2
    debug("Q2 ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), ": odd windows ", udec_(nOddWin[armIdx]), ", samples off the usual value ", udec_(nDev1[armIdx]), ", max |dev| ", udec_(maxDev1[armIdx]), ", x <> C*(L-g) ", udec_(nAcctBad[armIdx]))
    if nOddWin[armIdx] == 0
      bVaried := FALSE
    nAcct += nAcctBad[armIdx]
    worstDev := worstDev #> maxDev1[armIdx]
  if not bArmsOk
    debug("VERDICT Q2: INCONCLUSIVE - a Q2 arm failed its window control (RIG FAIL above)")
  elseif not bVaried
    debug("VERDICT Q2: INCONCLUSIVE - a SINC1 arm saw no odd window, so there was nothing to contrast")
  elseif nAcct <> 0
    debug("VERDICT Q2: REFUTED - ", udec_(nAcct), " SINC1 sample(s) differ from C*(window clocks)")
  elseif worstDev > abs calCx
    debug("VERDICT Q2: REFUTED - SINC1 deviated by ", udec_(worstDev), ", more than one term")
  else
    debug("VERDICT Q2: CONFIRMED - SINC1 shows no such outlier: every sample = C*(clocks in its window); each odd window reads exactly one term (", udec_(abs calCx), ", 1/n) off, on that sample alone (odd windows NPS ", udec_(nOddWin[ARM_NPS_S1]), ", NPL ", udec_(nOddWin[ARM_NPL_S1]), ", CHP ", udec_(nOddWin[ARM_CHP_S1]), ")")


PRI verdict_q3() | bArmsOk, bJitter, hugePct, outPct, devPct
' Q3: WAITX #1 WC before GETXACC with a power-of-two count -- huge noise in
' SINC2, at most one term in SINC1.

' Local Variables:
' @local bArmsOk - both jitter arms passed their SPREAD control
' @local bJitter - the read point actually moved in both jitter arms
' @local hugePct - JIT-S2 samples off by >= 1000 terms, percent
' @local outPct - JIT-S2 outliers, percent
' @local devPct - JIT-S1 samples off the usual value, percent

  bArmsOk := armOk[ARM_JIT_S1] and armOk[ARM_JIT_S2]
  bJitter := lenMax[ARM_JIT_S1] > lenMin[ARM_JIT_S1] and lenMax[ARM_JIT_S2] > lenMin[ARM_JIT_S2]
  hugePct := nHuge[ARM_JIT_S2] * PCT / (nDsamp[ARM_JIT_S2] #> 1)
  outPct := nOut[ARM_JIT_S2] * PCT / (nDsamp[ARM_JIT_S2] #> 1)
  devPct := nDev1[ARM_JIT_S1] * PCT / (arm_field(ARM_JIT_S1, AF_NS) - WARM)
  debug("Q3 JIT-S2: windows ", udec_(lenMin[ARM_JIT_S2]), "..", udec_(lenMax[ARM_JIT_S2]), "; outliers ", udec_(outPct), " % (predicted ~75), huge ", udec_(hugePct), " %, max |e| ", udec_(maxAbsErr[ARM_JIT_S2]), " | JIT-S1: off ", udec_(devPct), " % (predicted ~50), max |dev| ", udec_(maxDev1[ARM_JIT_S1]), ", x <> C*(L-g) ", udec_(nAcctBad[ARM_JIT_S1]), " | no-WC reference P2-S2 outliers ", udec_(nOut[ARM_P2_S2]))
  if not bArmsOk
    debug("VERDICT Q3: INCONCLUSIVE - a jitter arm failed its window control (RIG FAIL above)")
  elseif not bJitter
    debug("VERDICT Q3: INCONCLUSIVE - WAITX #1 WC did not move the read point (every window equal)")
  elseif nAcctBad[ARM_JIT_S1] <> 0 or maxDev1[ARM_JIT_S1] > abs calCx
    debug("VERDICT Q3: REFUTED - SINC1 under the same jitter is off by more than one term (max |dev| ", udec_(maxDev1[ARM_JIT_S1]), ")")
  elseif hugePct < JIT_REFUTE_PCT
    debug("VERDICT Q3: REFUTED - no huge noise: only ", udec_(hugePct), " % of SINC2 samples are off by >= 1000 terms")
  elseif hugePct >= JIT_CONFIRM_PCT and nOut[ARM_P2_S2] == 0
    debug("VERDICT Q3: CONFIRMED - 1 clock of read jitter: SINC2 ", udec_(hugePct), " % of samples off by >= 1000 terms (max ", udec_(maxAbsErr[ARM_JIT_S2]), "), SINC1 at most one term (", udec_(devPct), " % off by ", udec_(maxDev1[ARM_JIT_S1]), "); same loop without WC clean")
  else
    debug("VERDICT Q3: INCONCLUSIVE - SINC2 huge in ", udec_(hugePct), " % (between 5 and 25), or the no-WC reference was not clean")


PRI verdict_q4() | armIdx, twinIdx, bArmsOk, bConst, bClean, bTwins, pairIdx, nNorm
' Q4: XZERO instead of XCONT -- one window length and one unchanging SINC2
' sample, against XCONT twins that vary. Constancy, not C*n^2, is the XZERO
' test: g was measured on an XCONT loop.

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - XZERO arm index
' @local twinIdx - its XCONT twin
' @local bArmsOk - every Q4 arm passed its SPREAD control
' @local bConst - every XZERO arm kept one window length
' @local bClean - every XZERO arm's d never changed
' @local bTwins - every twin had odd windows and outliers
' @local pairIdx - which XZERO/twin pair, 0..Q4_PAIRS-1
' @local nNorm - the XZERO arm's usual active clocks per window

  bArmsOk := TRUE
  bConst := TRUE
  bClean := TRUE
  bTwins := TRUE
  repeat pairIdx from 0 to Q4_PAIRS - 1
    armIdx := lookupz(pairIdx : ARM_XZS_S2, ARM_XZC_S2, ARM_XZL_S2)
    twinIdx := lookupz(pairIdx : ARM_NPS_S2, ARM_CHP_S2, ARM_XCL_S2)
    nNorm := normLen[armIdx] - gapClocks
    debug("Q4 ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), ": windows ", udec_(lenMin[armIdx]), "..", udec_(lenMax[armIdx]), " clocks, d changed in ", udec_(nDvar[armIdx]), " of ", udec_(nDsamp[armIdx]), " (d(k=4) = ", sdec_(smp(armIdx, WARM + 1, SR_X) - smp(armIdx, WARM, SR_X)), ", C*n^2 = ", sdec_(calCx * nNorm * nNorm), ") | XCONT twin ", zstr_(arm_name(twinIdx)), ": odd windows ", udec_(nOddWin[twinIdx]), ", outliers ", udec_(nOut[twinIdx]))
    if not armOk[armIdx] or not armOk[twinIdx]
      bArmsOk := FALSE
    if lenMax[armIdx] <> lenMin[armIdx]
      bConst := FALSE
    if nDvar[armIdx] <> 0
      bClean := FALSE
    if nOddWin[twinIdx] == 0 or nOut[twinIdx] == 0
      bTwins := FALSE
  if not bArmsOk
    debug("VERDICT Q4: INCONCLUSIVE - a Q4 arm failed its window control (RIG FAIL above)")
  elseif not bConst
    debug("VERDICT Q4: REFUTED - XZERO did not keep one window length (see the Q4 lines above)")
  elseif not bClean
    debug("VERDICT Q4: INCONCLUSIVE - XZERO windows constant yet SINC2 samples changed: a different mechanism (first-stage range at that J?)")
  elseif not bTwins
    debug("VERDICT Q4: INCONCLUSIVE - an XCONT twin showed no odd window, so XZERO had nothing to avoid there")
  else
    debug("VERDICT Q4: CONFIRMED - XZERO kept one window length and an unchanging SINC2 sample at 10.24 us, 100 us and 25 ms measurements (streams 10.5 / 204.8 / 400 ms), where the XCONT twins varied and corrupted")


PRI q5_class(armIdx) : pLabel
' One-word class of an arm's model comparison, for the Q5 lines.
'
' @param armIdx - arm index, 0..NARMS-1
' @returns pLabel - address of the label

  if fitState[armIdx] <> FIT_OK
    pLabel := @s_nofit
  elseif nMisClean[armIdx] <> 0
    pLabel := @s_cleanmis
  elseif nMisOut[armIdx] <> 0
    pLabel := @s_outmis
  else
    pLabel := @s_modelok


PRI verdict_q5() | armIdx, bArmsOk, bFit, nClnMis, nOutMis, nOutTested, bP2AllOff
' Q5: does the carry model reproduce every sample, outliers included?

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index
' @local bArmsOk - every decisive arm passed its SPREAD control
' @local bFit - every decisive arm fitted exactly
' @local nClnMis - clean-window mismatches, decisive arms
' @local nOutMis - window-changed mismatches, decisive arms
' @local nOutTested - outliers compared, decisive arms
' @local bP2AllOff - every clean P2-S2 sample misses the model (C*n^2 fails)

  bArmsOk := TRUE
  bFit := TRUE
  nClnMis := 0
  nOutMis := 0
  nOutTested := 0
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    if is_sinc2(armIdx)
      debug("Q5 ", zstr_(arm_name(armIdx)), ": ", zstr_(q5_class(armIdx)), " - fit J ", sdec_(fitXterm[armIdx]), ", mismatches clean ", udec_(nMisClean[armIdx]), " / window-changed ", udec_(nMisOut[armIdx]), " (first k=", sdec_(firstMisK[armIdx]), "), outliers ", udec_(nOut[armIdx]))
  repeat armIdx from ARM_P2_S2 to ARM_JIT_S2
    if armIdx == ARM_P2_S2 or armIdx == ARM_NPS_S2 or armIdx == ARM_NPL_S2 or armIdx == ARM_JIT_S2
      if not armOk[armIdx]
        bArmsOk := FALSE
      if fitState[armIdx] <> FIT_OK
        bFit := FALSE
      nClnMis += nMisClean[armIdx]
      nOutMis += nMisOut[armIdx]
      nOutTested += nOut[armIdx]
  bP2AllOff := fitState[ARM_P2_S2] == FIT_OK and nMisClean[ARM_P2_S2] == nDsamp[ARM_P2_S2] - nChanged[ARM_P2_S2] and nMisClean[ARM_P2_S2] <> 0
  if not bArmsOk
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: INCONCLUSIVE - a decisive arm failed its window control (RIG FAIL above)")
  elseif not bFit
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: INCONCLUSIVE - the model fit was not exact in a decisive arm (see the fit lines)")
  elseif bP2AllOff
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: SEPARATE-MECHANISM - the clean prediction fails everywhere: P2-S2 reads d = ", sdec_(smp(ARM_P2_S2, WARM + 1, SR_X) - smp(ARM_P2_S2, WARM, SR_X)), ", the model C*n^2 = ", sdec_(calCx * P2_WINDOW * P2_WINDOW), " (d ~ 0 would mean GETXACC also clears the first stage)")
  elseif nClnMis <> 0
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: INCONCLUSIVE - the model broke at ", udec_(nClnMis), " clean-window sample(s) (premise failed; see first k and J above)")
  elseif nOutTested < MIN_OUT_Q5
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: INCONCLUSIVE - only ", udec_(nOutTested), " outliers to compare (need ", udec_(MIN_OUT_Q5), ")")
  elseif nOutMis <> 0
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: SEPARATE-MECHANISM - ", udec_(nOutMis), " window-changed sample(s) differ from the carry model while every clean-window sample matches (residuals in the MISMATCH rows)")
  else
    debug("VERDICT Q5 MECHANISM: CARRY-MODEL-MATCHES - all ", udec_(nOutTested), " outliers and every clean sample equal the model exactly (P2-S2, NPS-S2, NPL-S2, JIT-S2): each corruption is the first-stage integral J gained or lost by a +-1 window and returned by the next read")
  debug("Q5 corroboration (not deciding): CHP-S2 ", zstr_(q5_class(ARM_CHP_S2)), ", XZS-S2 ", zstr_(q5_class(ARM_XZS_S2)), ", XZC-S2 ", zstr_(q5_class(ARM_XZC_S2)), "; Y = 3*X mismatches in all arms: ", udec_(y_total()))


PRI y_total() : nBadTotal | armIdx
' Total Y-corroboration mismatches over every arm.
'
' @returns nBadTotal - sum of nYbad over the arms

' Local Variables:
' @local armIdx - arm index

  nBadTotal := 0
  repeat armIdx from 0 to NARMS - 1
    nBadTotal += nYbad[armIdx]


DAT ' ---- Labels ----
nm_p2s1         byte    "P2-S1 (SINC1, 256 clk/cycle, XCONT)", 0
nm_p2s2         byte    "P2-S2 (SINC2, 256 clk/cycle, XCONT)", 0
nm_nps1         byte    "NPS-S1 (SINC1, 2^23+64, XCONT)", 0
nm_nps2         byte    "NPS-S2 (SINC2, 2^23+64, XCONT)", 0
nm_npl1         byte    "NPL-S1 (SINC1, 2^23-64, XCONT)", 0
nm_npl2         byte    "NPL-S2 (SINC2, 2^23-64, XCONT)", 0
nm_chp1         byte    "CHP-S1 (SINC1, 1 MHz, 100 cycles, XCONT)", 0
nm_chp2         byte    "CHP-S2 (SINC2, 1 MHz, 100 cycles, XCONT)", 0
nm_jit1         byte    "JIT-S1 (SINC1, 256 clk/cycle, WAITX #1 WC)", 0
nm_jit2         byte    "JIT-S2 (SINC2, 256 clk/cycle, WAITX #1 WC)", 0
nm_xzs2         byte    "XZS-S2 (SINC2, 2^23+64, XZERO)", 0
nm_xzc2         byte    "XZC-S2 (SINC2, 1 MHz, 100 cycles, XZERO)", 0
nm_xzl2         byte    "XZL-S2 (SINC2, 1 MHz, 25000 cycles, XZERO)", 0
nm_xcl2         byte    "XCL-S2 (SINC2, 1 MHz, 25000 cycles, XCONT)", 0
s_match         byte    "MATCH", 0
s_mismatch      byte    "MISMATCH", 0
s_nofit         byte    "NO-FIT", 0
s_cleanmis      byte    "CLEAN-MISMATCH", 0
s_outmis        byte    "OUTLIER-MISMATCH", 0
s_modelok       byte    "MODEL-MATCH", 0


{ MEASURING ENGINE -- runs in its own cog; the ONLY code that touches the
  streamer. No debug() here (DEBUG_COGS excludes this cog anyway).
  PTRA = @mbox on entry. No SETQ precedes any XINIT/XCONT/XZERO, so every
  command runs at the SETXFRQ value set while the streamer was idle.
}
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Engine ----
engine          mov     mbase_, ptra
                setluts #0                      ' LUT sharing OFF (reset state)
                wrpin   #0, #PIN                ' P3: smart pin off, reset config
                drvl    #PIN                    ' P3 plain output

                ' the same long at all 512 LUT addresses, then read all back
                mov     idx_, #LUT_LAST
.fill           wrlut   lutv_, idx_
                djnf    idx_, #.fill
                mov     lutbad_, #0
                mov     idx_, #LUT_LAST
.chk            rdlut   tmp_, idx_
                cmp     tmp_, lutv_             wz
        if_nz   add     lutbad_, #1
                djnf    idx_, #.chk

                ' CAL: the per-clock term at P3 LOW, then P3 HIGH (SINC1, 1:1)
                setxfrq freq1to1_
                mov     ptrb, mbase_
                add     ptrb, #MB_CAL * 4
                drvl    #PIN
                waitx   ##WAIT_PIN
                call    #cal_one
                drvh    #PIN                    ' P3 HIGH from here to the end
                waitx   ##WAIT_PIN
                call    #cal_one

                ' the arms, in table order; records follow the header
                mov     ptrb, mbase_
                add     ptrb, #HDR * 4
                mov     armi_, #0
.arm            mov     rowp_, armi_
                mul     rowp_, #ARM_FIELDS
                add     rowp_, #arm_tab
                alts    rowp_
                mov     armf_, 0-0              ' AF_FREQ
                add     rowp_, #1
                alts    rowp_
                mov     dcmd_, 0-0              ' AF_CMD
                add     rowp_, #1
                alts    rowp_
                mov     kind_, 0-0              ' AF_KIND
                add     rowp_, #1
                alts    rowp_
                mov     ns_, 0-0                ' AF_NS
                call    #run_arm
                add     armi_, #1
                cmp     armi_, #NARMS           wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.arm

                mov     tmp_, mbase_
                add     tmp_, #MB_LUTBAD * 4
                wrlong  lutbad_, tmp_
                wrlong  #MBOX_DONE, mbase_      ' done -- always the last write
                cogid   tmp_
                cogstop tmp_                    ' releases P3

' CAL at the current P3 level: zero burst, B, 64-clock SINC1 burst, zero burst
' (flushes the EF-070 trailing term), R. R - B = 64*C. Reads are idle (EF-069:
' an idle GETXACC clears nothing).
cal_one         testp   #PIN                    wc
                wrc     tmp_
                wrlong  tmp_, ptrb++            ' CR_PIN
                xinit   dzero_, imz_            ' zero burst: first stage := 0
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc calb_                   ' B
                mov     calby_, 0-0
                xinit   dcal_, imk_             ' SINC1 burst, N_CAL active clocks
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                xinit   dzero_, imz_            ' flush the trailing term
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                getxacc calr_                   ' R
                mov     calry_, 0-0
                wrlong  calb_, ptrb++           ' CR_B
                wrlong  calby_, ptrb++          ' CR_BY
                wrlong  calr_, ptrb++           ' CR_R
                wrlong  calry_, ptrb++          ' CR_RY
                ret

' One arm: zero the first stage, set the arm's frequency while idle, XINIT,
' then ns_ reads in the loop the arm's kind selects. Each loop reads once per
' command, a fixed distance after the boundary its XCONT/XZERO waited for.
run_arm         mov     hdrp_, ptrb
                add     ptrb, #ARM_HDR * 4
                setxfrq freq1to1_
                xinit   dzero_, imz_            ' SINC1 zero burst: first stage := 0
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                setxfrq armf_                   ' the arm's frequency (streamer idle)
                testp   #PIN                    wc
                wrc     pinb_
                mov     cnt_, ns_
                getct   ct0_
                xinit   dcmd_, imk_             ' start the stream (zeroes phase)
                cmp     kind_, #KIND_JITTER     wz
        if_z    jmp     #loop_jit
                cmp     kind_, #KIND_XZERO      wz
        if_z    jmp     #loop_xz

loop_xc         xcont   dcmd_, imk_             ' waits for the running command's last clock
                waitx   #JIT_MASK               ' fixed 3 clocks
                getxacc xsum_
                mov     ysum_, 0-0
                getct   ctv_
                wrlong  xsum_, ptrb++           ' SR_X
                wrlong  ysum_, ptrb++           ' SR_Y
                wrlong  ctv_, ptrb++            ' SR_CT
                djnz    cnt_, #loop_xc
                jmp     #arm_end

loop_jit        xcont   dcmd_, imk_
                waitx   #JIT_MASK               wc      ' 2 + (1 AND RND): Chip's jitter
                getxacc xsum_
                mov     ysum_, 0-0
                getct   ctv_
                wrlong  xsum_, ptrb++
                wrlong  ysum_, ptrb++
                wrlong  ctv_, ptrb++
                djnz    cnt_, #loop_jit
                jmp     #arm_end

loop_xz         xzero   dcmd_, imk_             ' as XCONT, but zeroes phase per command
                waitx   #JIT_MASK
                getxacc xsum_
                mov     ysum_, 0-0
                getct   ctv_
                wrlong  xsum_, ptrb++
                wrlong  ysum_, ptrb++
                wrlong  ctv_, ptrb++
                djnz    cnt_, #loop_xz

arm_end         xstop                           ' XINIT #0,#0: stop now
                testp   #PIN                    wc
                wrc     pina_
                wrlong  ct0_, hdrp_             ' AH_CT0
                add     hdrp_, #4
                wrlong  pinb_, hdrp_            ' AH_PINB
                add     hdrp_, #4
                wrlong  pina_, hdrp_            ' AH_PINA
                add     hdrp_, #4
                wrlong  ns_, hdrp_              ' AH_NS
                waitx   ##WAIT_IDLE
                ret

freq1to1_       long    FREQ_1TO1
lutv_           long    LUTV
dzero_          long    MODE_S1 | ZCOUNT
dcal_           long    MODE_S1 | N_CAL
imk_            long    IMM_K
imz_            long    IMM_Z

' one row per arm: AF_FREQ, AF_CMD, AF_KIND, AF_NS -- order MUST match ARM_xxx
arm_tab         long    FREQ_P2,   MODE_S1 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XCONT,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_P2_S1
                long    FREQ_P2,   MODE_S2 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XCONT,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_P2_S2
                long    FREQ_NPS,  MODE_S1 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XCONT,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_NPS_S1
                long    FREQ_NPS,  MODE_S2 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XCONT,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_NPS_S2
                long    FREQ_NPL,  MODE_S1 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XCONT,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_NPL_S1
                long    FREQ_NPL,  MODE_S2 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XCONT,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_NPL_S2
                long    FREQ_CHIP, MODE_S1 | CYC_CHIP, KIND_XCONT,  NS_CHIP     ' ARM_CHP_S1
                long    FREQ_CHIP, MODE_S2 | CYC_CHIP, KIND_XCONT,  NS_CHIP     ' ARM_CHP_S2
                long    FREQ_P2,   MODE_S1 | CYC_FAST, KIND_JITTER, NS_FAST     ' ARM_JIT_S1
                long    FREQ_P2,   MODE_S2 | CYC_FAST, KIND_JITTER, NS_FAST     ' ARM_JIT_S2
                long    FREQ_NPS,  MODE_S2 | CYC_FAST, KIND_XZERO,  NS_FAST     ' ARM_XZS_S2
                long    FREQ_CHIP, MODE_S2 | CYC_CHIP, KIND_XZERO,  NS_CHIP     ' ARM_XZC_S2
                long    FREQ_CHIP, MODE_S2 | CYC_LONG, KIND_XZERO,  NS_LONG     ' ARM_XZL_S2
                long    FREQ_CHIP, MODE_S2 | CYC_LONG, KIND_XCONT,  NS_LONG     ' ARM_XCL_S2

mbase_          res     1
idx_            res     1
tmp_            res     1
lutbad_         res     1
armi_           res     1
rowp_           res     1
armf_           res     1
dcmd_           res     1
kind_           res     1
ns_             res     1
cnt_            res     1
hdrp_           res     1
ct0_            res     1
pinb_           res     1
pina_           res     1
xsum_           res     1
ysum_           res     1
ctv_            res     1
calb_           res     1
calby_          res     1
calr_           res     1
calry_          res     1

